import{_ as o,o as t,c as a,a2 as s}from"./chunks/framework.BN3Eol-0.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"UXD-027 — Explore levels: one shell table, glyphs in the level picker and the nav, a \\"what you are looking at\\" card, and one welcome hint","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"uxs/decisions/UXD-027-explore-levels-one-table-glyphs-card-and-hint.md","filePath":"uxs/decisions/UXD-027-explore-levels-one-table-glyphs-card-and-hint.md"}'),n={name:"uxs/decisions/UXD-027-explore-levels-one-table-glyphs-card-and-hint.md"};function d(r,e,l,c,i,h){return t(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<h1 id="uxd-027-—-explore-levels-one-shell-table-glyphs-in-the-level-picker-and-the-nav-a-what-you-are-looking-at-card-and-one-welcome-hint" tabindex="-1">UXD-027 — Explore levels: one shell table, glyphs in the level picker and the nav, a &quot;what you are looking at&quot; card, and one welcome hint <a class="header-anchor" href="#uxd-027-—-explore-levels-one-shell-table-glyphs-in-the-level-picker-and-the-nav-a-what-you-are-looking-at-card-and-one-welcome-hint" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;UXD-027 — Explore levels: one shell table, glyphs in the level picker and the nav, a &quot;what you are looking at&quot; card, and one welcome hint&quot;">​</a></h1><ul><li><strong>Status</strong>: accepted (built; the e2e counts are in Verification, a real device is open)</li><li><strong>Date</strong>: 2026-11-13 (proposed and decided)</li><li><strong>Decider</strong>: the operator, 2026-11-13 — all 6 recommendations of <code>docs/wip/2026-11-13-slice-C8-brief.md</code> §12 approved as written (&quot;I am OK on 25 recommendations&quot;, commit <code>ec0ceeb9be2</code>, for C6 to C10 together). This record is also the answer to the plan&#39;s <strong>D4</strong> (the second-level nav under Explore): <strong>keep it</strong>.</li><li><strong>Answers</strong>: E1, W1, E7, E9, E10 of the UX feedback plan; slice C8; D4</li><li><strong>Builds on</strong>: <a href="./UXD-021-explore-hud-scale-bar-picker-pills-references">UXD-021</a> (the level picker, the navigator row and its clearance of a docked panel, kept), <a href="./UXD-014-one-chip-and-filter">UXD-014</a> (the picker&#39;s chip and rungs stay <code>Chip</code>; a control that is not a chip is a 24 px <code>.ui-hit</code>), <a href="./UXD-016-compact-nav-and-more-menu">UXD-016</a> (the nav&#39;s compact rows and 32 / 44 px rules), <a href="./UXD-022-science-link-lists">UXD-022</a> (at most five <code>/science</code> links, deduped, in order), <a href="./UXD-024-orbit-ruler-one-row-draws-its-regime">UXD-024</a> (the disclosure-button pattern, the bottom-left column the hint stays out of)</li><li><strong>Changes</strong>: <code>src/lib/explore/scale-shells.ts</code> (new, with its test), <code>science-titles.ts</code> (new), <code>lens-panel.ts</code>, <code>src/lib/components/ScaleGlyph.svelte</code> (an <code>idSuffix</code>), <code>ScaleGlyphIcon.svelte</code>, <code>LevelContextCard.svelte</code>, <code>ExploreHint.svelte</code> (new), <code>src/lib/hint-state.ts</code> (new, with its test), <code>ExploreScalePicker.svelte</code>, <code>Nav.svelte</code>, <code>src/routes/+page.svelte</code>, <code>src/routes/explore/hub/+page.svelte</code>, <code>src/routes/explore/+page.svelte</code>, <code>src/lib/surface-scene/SurfaceScene.svelte</code>, <code>messages/*.json</code> (4 keys added), <code>tests/e2e/explore-level-card.spec.ts</code> (new), <code>explore-hint.spec.ts</code> (new), <code>explore-scale-picker.spec.ts</code>, <code>explore-science-lens-shells.spec.ts</code>, <code>nav-controls.spec.ts</code>, <code>footer-dock.spec.ts</code>; <a href="./../UXS-014">UXS-014</a>, <a href="./../IA">IA</a>, <code>docs/concept/05_Design_System.md</code>, <code>docs/adr/TA.md</code>, <code>docs/accessibility.md</code>, the module READMEs</li></ul><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Context&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The eight scale levels were written out by hand in five places: the nav dropdown (<code>Nav.svelte</code>), the Explore hub, the home grid, the level picker (a <code>labelFor</code> switch) and the Science Lens story (<code>lens-panel.ts</code>), each with its own copy of the <code>?context=</code> query, the name key and the description key. The home grid and the hub drew a glyph per level (<code>ScaleGlyph</code>); the nav and the picker drew none (the picker chip had a 6 px dot). The per-level story existed only inside the Science Lens panel, shown when the lens is on. Nothing on <code>/explore</code> or the Worlds invited the viewer to zoom. <a href="./../UXS-014">UXS-014</a> and TA still described a breadcrumb that was retired in #45: the &quot;breadcrumb&quot; of E10 is the level picker (the <code>◉ &lt;level&gt; ▾</code> chip and its ladder).</p><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Decision&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>One table (E7).</strong> <code>SCALE_SHELLS</code> (<code>src/lib/explore/scale-shells.ts</code>, typed on <code>ShellId</code>, order <code>CTX_ORDER</code>): per level the <code>?context=</code> query, the glyph id, <code>name</code>, <code>navName</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>desc</code>, the Science Lens story (<code>storyTitle</code>, <code>storyBody</code>) and up to five <code>tab/section</code> slugs. The nav dropdown, the hub, the home grid, the picker, the back-chip label (<code>scaleNavBackTarget</code>), the card and <code>computeLensPanel</code> map over it. Every message key is one that was already in use: no text was renamed or deleted (decision 6 of the brief: the three <code>explore_hub_shortcut_*</code> titles stay as the hub and home-grid <code>title</code>; the card and the lens use the story title). <code>navName</code> is the name except for the Solar System, where the nav and the hub say &quot;Explore&quot; (<code>nav_explore</code>), as before. The hub&#39;s Solar System tile keeps its bare <code>/explore</code> link (no query); the nav and the home grid keep <code>?context=solar-system</code>. A unit test fails when a level is missing, a glyph is unknown, a slug is not in <code>science-index.json</code>, a list is longer than five, two levels share a list, or a consumer file names a level&#39;s keys itself.</li><li><strong>D4: keep the second-level nav.</strong> The Explore dropdown stays (eight rows, the TV hub link, the mobile drawer group), built from the table. The levels are not pages: they are <code>?context=</code> on one prerendered <code>/explore</code> (the sitemap lists <code>/explore</code> and <code>/explore/hub</code>, unchanged). Not taken: dropping the dropdown (nothing is lost for keyboard, TV or direct-jump users by keeping it), and a real page per level (a routing and SEO change).</li><li><strong>Glyphs (E10).</strong> The picker&#39;s chip leads with the current level&#39;s glyph (20 px, in place of the 6 px dot) and every rung with its glyph (24 px), the same drawing the home grid and hub show (<code>ScaleGlyph</code>). A glyph needs gradient <code>&lt;defs&gt;</code> that sat in the two pages that drew it; <code>ScaleGlyphIcon</code> draws the glyph in its own <code>&lt;svg&gt;</code> with its own defs under ids suffixed per instance (<code>$props.id()</code>), so it works on any page and nine of them side by side share no id (<code>ScaleGlyph</code> got an optional <code>idSuffix</code>; the home grid and hub keep the page-wide defs, unchanged). With a pointer (<code>hover: hover</code>, <code>pointer: fine</code>, 700 px or wider) a rung also shows the home-grid <code>desc</code> under its name, one line cut with an ellipsis (15 rem) and linked as its <code>aria-describedby</code>; a phone or a coarse pointer shows glyph and name only. The Explore nav dropdown rows and the mobile drawer group lead with a 20 px glyph (decision 2a of the brief); the accessible name of a row is unchanged (the glyph is <code>aria-hidden</code>).</li><li><strong>The card (E9).</strong> <code>LevelContextCard</code> hangs under the picker row, at the right edge, 280 px wide (<code>max-width: 100vw - 16px</code>), left of a docked panel by the same <code>panelCoverPx + 8</code> as the row. Header: the level&#39;s glyph (24 px), its name, a fold button (<code>aria-expanded</code>, <code>aria-controls</code>; the TierContextCard pattern: 44 px target, <code>#889fe7</code> hover and focus). Body: what the level is (the home-grid <code>desc</code>, 90 % white), the story the lens used to carry (<code>explore_lens_story_*_body</code>, label grey), then up to five <code>/science/&lt;tab&gt;/&lt;section&gt;</code> links with the sections&#39; titles from <code>science-index.&lt;locale&gt;.json</code> (one fetch per locale, kept; the links are drawn once it has answered, so no slug flashes; if it cannot be read they read as their slugs; each link is a 24 px target, 44 px on touch). It follows the level and is drawn wherever the picker is: not in 2D, a black-hole or deep-sky takeover, or a body scene. Open with a pointer in a window 900 px wide and 560 px tall or more; folded on touch and in a smaller window with a mouse (found by the footer-dock sweep: at 375 x 812, 667 x 375 and 800 x 375 an open card met the chip rows and the scale panel); the choice is remembered (<code>localStorage</code> <code>orrery.explore.levelCardExpanded</code>, blocked storage falls back to the default). Folded, the card is only its header, as wide as that (in a small window with a mouse, only the glyph and the fold button: the picker chip above it names the level). The HUD chip row still stops only before the picker row (not the card): taking the card&#39;s 280 px made the layer chips wrap and move when a panel docked (chip-row spec), and folded in a small window the card is narrower than the row. The fold button is a disclosure, not a chip, and carries <code>data-a4-keep</code> (the chip sweep&#39;s documented exception; the orbit ruler header&#39;s pattern). It is a <code>section</code> named by the level. z 7, under the picker&#39;s open ladder (46) and under panels (30). The lists are curated per level in the table; no two are alike (Virgo and the Cosmic web open on the same section by design). &quot;A dedicated article per layer&quot; is a content task: the sections linked are the ones that exist, and the Virgo and Cosmic web levels still lack their own article.</li><li><strong>The story leaves the lens.</strong> Where the card is shown, <code>ScienceLayersPanel</code> no longer gets the story props, so the same paragraph is not on screen twice; it keeps its layer toggles and the solar system&#39;s historical foundations. A level with no layers (Local Group to Cosmic Web) therefore has no lens panel at all (the panel already hid itself with neither story nor layers). In a takeover (black hole, body scene) the picker and card are hidden and the panel keeps its story.</li><li><strong>One welcome hint (E1, W1).</strong> <code>ExploreHint</code>: a one-line dismissible status strip (<code>role=&quot;status&quot;</code>, <code>aria-live=&quot;polite&quot;</code>, the × is a 24 px <code>.ui-hit</code>, 44 px on touch, label <code>explore_anon_dismiss</code>), 11 px mono, the card&#39;s chrome. The same component on <code>/explore</code> (&quot;Zoom in or out through the 8 scales · drag to look around&quot;) and, once, in <code>SurfaceScene</code> for <code>/earth /moon /mars /venus</code> (&quot;Zoom in to explore · drag to look around&quot;). It goes at the first wheel turn, pinch or tap, or a drag of 6 px or more, <strong>on the canvas</strong>, at the ×, or after 12 s (on <code>/explore</code> a docked side panel also ends it: it is not drawn beside one and does not return when the panel closes; the page, and for the Worlds <code>SurfaceScene</code>, keeps a <code>hintDone</code> flag set by the hint&#39;s <code>ondismiss</code>, so a 2D or panorama toggle or a takeover does not bring it back either; the 12 s timer reports the timeout itself rather than a measured time, which could read just under 12 s); it fades over 300 ms (a CSS transition, so <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> cuts it) and is not remembered: it is back on the next visit (decision 5a of the brief). Pure rules in <code>src/lib/hint-state.ts</code>. A pointer device: bottom centre, 64 px up (on the Worlds above the nation legend); in a window under 900 px wide or 560 px tall it hangs left-aligned at 40 % of the scene&#39;s height, 48 px in (clear of the INDEX tab) and, from 600 px wide, ending before the scale strip. A touch device: under the top row (<code>top: 110px</code>), because the bottom edge is the scale strip, the time dock and the tab row. W1&#39;s &quot;a few locations at the start zoom&quot; is <strong>not</strong> built: the Worlds scene change is left to the Worlds slices (decision 4a).</li><li><strong>Four new keys, 14 locales, by hand.</strong> <code>explore_hint_zoom</code>, <code>surface_hint_zoom</code>, <code>explore_level_card_collapse_aria</code>, <code>explore_level_card_expand_aria</code>. The brief proposed reusing <code>surface_card_collapse_aria</code> / <code>surface_card_expand_aria</code> for the card&#39;s fold; their text is &quot;Collapse site details&quot;, wrong for a scale level, so the card has its own pair (&quot;Collapse scale details&quot;). The hint&#39;s close button reuses <code>explore_anon_dismiss</code>. The hint&#39;s &quot;8&quot; is a digit in every locale.</li></ol><h2 id="alternatives-not-taken" tabindex="-1">Alternatives not taken <a class="header-anchor" href="#alternatives-not-taken" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Alternatives not taken&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Dropping the Explore dropdown; a real route per level; the card at the bottom left (it competes with the ruler and the scale strip) or as the first block of the lens panel (visible only with the lens on, the present problem); a hint stored after its first dismissal; the Worlds scene markers at the start zoom (a scene change); deleting the three <code>explore_hub_shortcut_*</code> keys; <code>getScienceSection</code> per link for the titles (five overlay fetches against one small index).</p><h2 id="consequences" tabindex="-1">Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequences" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Consequences&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Adding a ninth level, or renaming one, is one edit in <code>scale-shells.ts</code> (plus its messages and glyph).</li><li><code>Nav.svelte</code> now imports the table and <code>ScaleGlyphIcon</code>, so the glyph code and the level messages load on every page.</li><li><code>/explore</code> shows a card at the top right at every level; with a right-docked panel it moves left of it.</li><li>A level with no layers has no Science Lens panel, and the panel registers the lens as available only while it has a story or layers to draw, so the Nav&#39;s toggle reads &quot;unavailable here&quot; (disabled) on Local Group to Cosmic Web (e2e).</li><li>The nine glyphs in the open ladder, the chip and the card are separate SVG documents with their own defs (five small gradients each).</li></ul><h2 id="verification" tabindex="-1">Verification <a class="header-anchor" href="#verification" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Verification&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Unit: <code>scale-shells.test.ts</code> (one record per level in ladder order, glyphs known, <code>?context=</code> queries, at most five slugs that are in <code>science-index.json</code>, no repeats, no two levels alike, the lens story is the table&#39;s, no consumer file carries a level&#39;s keys), <code>hint-state.test.ts</code> (wheel, pinch, tap, close, a drag only past 6 px, 12 s), <code>lens-panel.test.ts</code> (unchanged, green). E2E, <code>explore-level-card.spec.ts</code> (new: the eight levels&#39; name, lead, one to five <code>/science</code> links and one glyph; the links read as titles; the fold, its memory across a reload and across levels; the card follows a jump through the picker; hidden in 2D and in a black-hole takeover; the card and a docked Jupiter panel disjoint at 1280 x 720), <code>explore-hint.spec.ts</code> (new: <code>/explore</code> and the four Worlds show it, a wheel on the canvas ends it, it is back on reload, the × closes it, a tap keeps it and a drag ends it), <code>explore-scale-picker.spec.ts</code> (a glyph in the chip and in each of the eight rungs, the rungs in ladder order, no duplicate id), <code>explore-science-lens-shells.spec.ts</code> (the story is the card&#39;s, no lens panel on a level without layers), <code>nav-controls.spec.ts</code> (the Explore group: eight rows in order, each with a glyph, the live level active), <code>footer-dock.spec.ts</code> (the card and the hint among the HUD parts). The run counts and the screenshots are in the C8 row of <code>CHANGE-INVENTORY.md</code>.</p><h2 id="not-covered" tabindex="-1">Not covered <a class="header-anchor" href="#not-covered" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Not covered&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A real device; a production build; the 12 s timeout in a browser (unit-tested only); the card and hint in ja, ko, zh-CN, hi and ru (de and ar were read); the Worlds hint over a phone&#39;s bottom bar in a browser with real WebGL; the card at the solar system with the ladder open, over the card&#39;s lower edge (the ladder is above it by design).</p>',14)])])}const g=o(n,[["render",d]]);export{u as __pageData,g as default};
